    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d245">

                <pb facs="0446" n="428" sameAs="frus:frus1947v03/pg428"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.50 Recovery/9–1247: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-09-12T16:00:00+01:00">September 12,
                            1947—4 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3714. At a meeting last night of the entire Committee of Cooperation the
                    delegates were informed by Franks of the results of our meeting with the
                    Executive Committee, reported my 3709, September 12, 1 p. m. The Cooperation
                    Committee decided to postpone the formal meeting of the conference called to
                    receive the report until September 20–22, the exact date to be determined
                    later.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 3714, repeated London for Clayton and Douglas 729.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
